@prefix ldh:    <https://w3id.org/atomgraph/linkeddatahub#> .
@prefix rdf:    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix dh:     <https://www.w3.org/ns/ldt/document-hierarchy#> .
@prefix dct:    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<> a dh:Item ;
    dct:title "Upload file" ;
    dct:description "Learn how to upload files to LinkedDataHub" ;
    rdf:_1 <#content> .

<#content> a ldh:XHTML ;
    rdf:value """<div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <p class="lead">Learn how to upload files to LinkedDataHub</p>
    <div>
        <h2 id="upload">Upload a file</h2>
        <div class="ldhc-tabs or-horizontal">
            <div class="ldhc-tablist sz-md va-line" role="tablist">
                <button aria-controls="user-interface-pane" aria-selected="true" class="ldhc-tab is-on" id="user-interface-tab" role="tab" type="button"><span class="ldhc-tab-lbl">User interface</span></button>
                <button aria-controls="command-line-interface-pane" aria-selected="false" class="ldhc-tab" id="command-line-interface-tab" role="tab" type="button"><span class="ldhc-tab-lbl">Command line interface</span></button>
            </div>
            <div aria-labelledby="user-interface-tab" class="ldhc-tabpanel" id="user-interface-pane" role="tabpanel">
                    <div>
                        <ol>
                            <li>Click the <span class="btn btn-primary create-action">Create <span class="caret"></span></span> dropdown at the bottom of the page</li>
                            <li>Click on <samp>File</samp> in the dropdown list that appears</li>
                            <li>Fill out the mandatory <dfn>File</dfn> fields in the form:
                                <dl>
                                    <dt>Filename</dt>
                                    <dd>Select file from your filesystem</dd>
                                    <dt>Title</dt>
                                    <dd>Enter file title</dd>
                                </dl>
                            </li>
                            <li>Click <span class="btn btn-primary btn-save">Save</span></li>
                        </ol>
                        <div class="screenshot-placeholder">
                            <span aria-hidden="true" class="msi">play_circle</span>
                            <p>Screen recording: uploading a file</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            <div aria-labelledby="command-line-interface-tab" class="ldhc-tabpanel" hidden="hidden" id="command-line-interface-pane" role="tabpanel">
                    <div>
                        <p>A file is uploaded to the document that will hold it, so create that document first. Uploading Nancy Davolio's portrait from the Northwind demo:</p>
                        <pre>doc=$(ldh create-item \\
  --title "Nancy Davolio" \\
  --container "${LDH_BASE}employees/")

ldh add-file \\
  --title "Nancy Davolio" \\
  --file employees/nancy.jpg \\
  --content-type "image/jpeg" \\
  "$doc"</pre>
                        <p>The command prints the content-addressed URI of the upload as its only output:</p>
                        <pre>https://localhost:4443/uploads/fb2e87988887cebf252947ba5d98e34d01d44ed4</pre>
                        <p>That URI is stable across instances — it is derived from the file content alone — which is what lets the
                            <a href="../../tutorial/media/" target="_blank">Northwind CSVs</a> reference their images by hash before they are even uploaded.
                            <code>--content-type</code> is optional — the media type is detected from the file when it is not given.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="alert alert-warning">
        <p><strong>Note about ontology files</strong></p>
        <p>If you upload an ontology file (RDF/OWL), be aware that it will not be automatically loaded via <code>owl:imports</code> declarations.
        This is deliberate: resolving imports at upload time would risk circular dependencies during system initialization.</p>
        <p>For more information on working with ontologies, see the <a href="../../reference/administration/ontologies/">ontologies reference documentation</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="lead"><a href="../../reference/dataset/#hierarchical-uris" target="_blank">Read more about the content-addressed uploads namespace.</a></p>
</div>"""^^rdf:XMLLiteral .
